From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0187: clear CS_RESTRICT for the window server

dyld ignores DYLD_* when the process carries CS_RESTRICT, which a platform
binary's signature has. This port marks its binaries as platform ones; the
reference port does not, and needs no such clearing.

---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5805,6 +5805,14 @@
 		 * environment injected by 0175 reaches it.
 		 */
 		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~CS_PLATFORM_BINARY;
+		/*
+		 * dyld discards DYLD_* for a process that carries CS_RESTRICT, and the
+		 * signature of a platform binary carries it: kern_exec inherits it above.
+		 * The hakios kernel never marks these binaries as platform ones, so it
+		 * never has the problem; clearing the inherited flags here does the same.
+		 */
+		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~(CS_RESTRICT | CS_HARD | CS_KILL | CS_ENFORCEMENT | CS_FORCED_LV);
+		printf("sweet: backboardd carries no CS_RESTRICT; dyld will read its environment\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd is not a platform binary; dyld reads its environment\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd may load a library that is not Apple's\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd is marked debuggable so dyld takes its DYLD_* variables\n");
